E("sankardev","Srimanta Sankardev","Saints of the bhakti movement",1449,1568,"1449–1568 (traditional)","Saint, poet and reformer","Founder of the Ekasarana bhakti movement and a defining figure of Assamese literature, music and dance. Wrote the Kirtana-ghosha, borgeets and Ankia Naat plays.","Scholars give his death as 1569. Wives: Suryava and Kalindi; son Ramananda.",("sankar",),"high",("Srimanta Sankardev",),"শ্ৰীমন্ত শংকৰদেৱ",era="bhakti",birth=1449,death=1568)
E("madhavdev","Madhavdev","Saints of the bhakti movement",1489,1596,"1489–1596","Saint and poet","Sankardev's chief disciple and successor, converted after a debate around 1532. Wrote the Naam Ghosa and about 191 borgeets.","",("madhav",),"high",as_="মাধৱদেৱ",era="bhakti",birth=1489,death=1596)
