E("samudrapala","Samudrapala","Kamarupa after the Palas",1100,1110,"c. 1100 (no dates given)","Ruler of Kamarupa","Listed as ruling Kamarupa proper after Jayapala; no dates or events are given.","",("kamarupa",),"low",sort=1101)
E("ramapala","Ramapala (Pala Empire of Bengal)","Pala Empire of Bengal",1100,1126,"c. 1072–1126 (sources vary)","Pala emperor of Bengal","Conquered western Kamarupa and installed Timgyadeva as governor. Sources differ on whether he took only parts of north Bengal or Kamarupa itself.","Reign given as 1072–1126 or 1077–1133.",("kamarupa","palakam"),"medium",sort=1105)
E("timgyadeva","Timgyadeva","Kamarupa after the Palas",1110,1126,"c. 1110–1126","Governor and ruler of western Kamarupa","Made governor of Kamarupa by Ramapala, ruling from Hamshkonchi; later rebelled and ruled independently until he was replaced.","The claim that he threw off Pala rule is marked as needing a citation.",("palakam","kamarupa"),"medium")
E("kumarapala-bengal","Kumarapala (Pala king of Bengal)","Pala Empire of Bengal",1126,1130,"early 12th century","Pala king of Bengal","Sent Vaidyadeva to put down Timgyadeva's rebellion in Kamarupa and kept friendly relations with him.","Some accounts call him Timgyadeva's son, which looks like a mistake; he is Ramapala's son.",("kamarupa","palakam"),"low",sort=1126)
E("vaidyadeva","Vaidyadeva","Kamarupa after the Palas",1126,1140,"c. 1126–1140","Ruler of western Kamarupa","Replaced Timgyadeva under Kumarapala, then in effect created a separate kingdom after Kumarapala's death. Issued grants in the old Kamarupa style under the elephant seal and took the title Maharajadhiraja.","The Kamauli plates date his fourth year while governing under Kumarapala.",("palakam","kamarupa"),"medium")
E("bhaskara-lunar","Bhaskara (lunar dynasty)","Kamarupa after the Palas",1120,1140,"c. 1120–1200 (dynasty)","Ruler of central Kamarupa","First of a “lunar dynasty” known from one 1185 inscription; held parts of Kamrup, Darrang and Sonitpur on the north bank.","No individual dates; the four rulers share the span 1120–1200.",("kamarupa",),"low",sort=1120)
E("rayarideva","Rayarideva","Kamarupa after the Palas",1140,1170,"12th century","Ruler of central Kamarupa","Member of the lunar dynasty of the north bank, known only from the 1185 inscription.","",("kamarupa",),"low",sort=1145)
E("udayakarna","Udayakarna","Kamarupa after the Palas",1170,1185,"12th century (inscription 1185)","Ruler of central Kamarupa","Member of the lunar dynasty known from the 1185 inscription.","",("kamarupa",),"low",sort=1170)
