# --- Delhi and Bengal sultanate figures who touch Assam
E("ghiyasuddin-iwaz-khalji","Ghiyasuddin Iwaz Khalji","Sultanate and Mughal figures",1226,1228,"1226–1228","Sultan of Bengal","Invaded Kamarupa in 1226–27, was worsted near Nagaon and withdrew to Lakhnauti, where he was captured and killed in 1227–28 by Nasiruddin Mahmud.","",("mik","kamarupa"),"medium",era="early-ahom")
E("nasiruddin-mahmud","Nasiruddin Mahmud","Sultanate and Mughal figures",1228,1229,"1228–1229","Delhi prince and governor","Son of Iltutmish; took Bengal after Iwaz Khalji, entered Kamarupa and installed a tributary king who lost control after Nasiruddin's death in 1229.","",("mik","kamarupa"),"medium")
E("ghiyasuddin-bahadur-shah","Ghiyasuddin Bahadur Shah","Sultanate and Mughal figures",1321,1322,"raid 1321–1322; d. 1327–28","Sultan of Sonargaon","Raided Kamata as far as Nagaon, meeting ineffective resistance from Pratapdhwaj and the Kacharis, but kept no territory. Killed by Muhammad Tughlaq in 1327–28.","",("mik","bkw"),"medium")
E("shamsuddin-ilyas-shah","Shamsuddin Ilyas Shah","Sultanate and Mughal figures",1356,1357,"d. c. November 1357","Sultan of Bengal","His forces advanced up the Brahmaputra and occupied Kamrup, including Guwahati, before his death around November 1357.","",("mik","bkw"),"medium")
E("sikandar-shah-bengal","Sikandar Shah of Bengal","Sultanate and Mughal figures",1357,1362,"expeditions 1357–1362","Sultan of Bengal","Advanced to the Kopili river, where Kamata, Bhuyan and Barahi forces fought him near Gachtal. Silver coins of 1360 carry a Kamrup mint name, but how long he held it is unclear.","The outcome of the Gachtal fighting is not stated in the article.",("mik","bkw"),"medium")
E("ghiyasuddin-azam-shah","Ghiyasuddin Azam Shah","Sultanate and Mughal figures",1396,1400,"c. 1396–1400 (reign 1389–1410)","Sultan of Bengal","An inscription at Boko in Kamrup shows the Sultanate held the region for some years. The Kamata king, allied with the Ahoms by marriage, drove him back across the Karatoya.","Dates are inferred from coins.",("mik","bkw"),"medium")
E("shamsuddin-muzaffar-shah","Shamsuddin Muzaffar Shah","Sultanate and Mughal figures",1492,1493,"1492–1493","Sultan of Bengal","Invaded Kamata and took parts of it, issuing coins with the title Kamata Mardan, before Husain Shah.","",("khen",),"medium")
E("shah-ismail-ghazi","Shah Ismail Ghazi","Sultanate and Mughal figures",1498,1499,"1498–1499","Commander of Husain Shah","Led about 24,000 men and a river flotilla to besiege and destroy Kamatapur and capture Nilambar.","",("bkw","nilambar"),"medium")
E("danyal","Shahzada Danyal","Sultanate and Mughal figures",1502,1510,"c. 1502–c. 1510","Governor of the conquered Kamata region","Husain Shah's son, made governor of the territory up to Hajo; the Bhuyans under Harup Narayan overran his garrison and ended Sultanate rule within about ten years.","",("bkw","kamata"),"medium")
E("sachipatra","Sachipatra","Kamata and Khen kingdoms",1498,1498,"1498 (traditional)","Brahmin minister","In the traditional account, a minister whose son Nilambar executed for an affair with the queen; said to have urged Husain Shah to invade. Escaped and was never heard of again.","Traditional, not independently documented.",("nilambar","bkw"),"low")

